/* Fill guess with attacker's guess */
memcpy(guess, secret, sizeof(guess));
/* Compare without leaking timing information */
if (ct_memcmp(secret, guess, sizeof(secret)) == 0) {
    /* secret matches guess – safe to proceed */
} else {
    /* secret does not match – abort operation */
}
```
By ensuring the comparison runs in constant time, an attacker cannot infer how many leading bytes match by measuring execution time.

